                <section id="plans">
                    <h2>3. Plans, billing and payments</h2>
                    <p>
                        CloudHub offers hosting plans, including a free Starter plan and paid plans.
                        The current plans, prices and limits are shown on our website. Prices are in South African rand (ZAR) per month.
                    </p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Limits.</strong> Each plan includes limits such as the number of projects and storage. You may not exceed the limits of your plan.</li>
                        <li><strong>Changing plans.</strong> You can upgrade at any time. You can downgrade only if your projects and storage fit within the smaller plan. Plan changes are recorded on your account.</li>
                        <li><strong>Cancelling.</strong> You can cancel a paid subscription from your billing page. Unless the law requires otherwise, cancelling stops future billing and does not refund the current billing period.</li>
                        <li><strong>Payments.</strong> Payments are processed by a third-party payment provider. A paid subscription is activated only once the provider confirms your payment to us, not simply because you returned from the checkout page.</li>
                        <li><strong>Invoices.</strong> We issue an invoice for each billing period. Failed or overdue payments may lead to your subscription being suspended or expiring.</li>
                        <li><strong>Price changes.</strong> We may change plan prices and limits. We will give you reasonable notice before a change affects your subscription.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>Nothing in this section limits any rights you have under the Consumer Protection Act 68 of 2008 or other South African law.</p>
                </section>

