                <section id="deployments">
                    <h2>5. Deployments</h2>
                    <p>You can deploy from a connected GitHub repository, from Visual Studio, or by uploading a ZIP package. When you deploy:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>We validate uploaded packages and may reject files that are unsafe, too large or unsupported.</li>
                        <li>Builds run on separate, isolated deployment workers and not on the main CloudHub web application.</li>
                        <li>Each deployment has a recorded status and log. A deployment is marked successful, and a public address is shown, only after the hosting environment confirms that your application is running.</li>
                        <li>A build or deployment can fail, for example because of errors in your code. We do not promise that every deployment will succeed.</li>
                        <li>You may only deploy repositories and code that you are authorised to use.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

